@startuml
title Release Evidence and Public-Claim Boundary

actor "Release maintainer" as maintainer
actor "Pull request author" as author
artifact "Changed production source" as productionDiff
artifact "Changed written specification" as specificationDiff
artifact "Changed native executable test" as nativeTestDiff
component "Strict PR verification report" as prVerification
component "Direct change contract\n(path-level minimum)" as directChangeContract
component "Runtime communications\nconformance gate" as runtimeCommsGate
node "Real Mosquitto broker\n+ mosquitto_sub client" as mosquitto
component "GitHub Release workflow" as release
component "Release candidate guard" as releaseGuard
component "Rust xtask external unsafe gate\nproduction + exact registered test inventory\nownership and stale-site decision" as unsafeGate
artifact "ast-grep / rg raw facts\nretained normalized and rejected sites" as unsafeFacts
component "Docs capture launcher" as captureLauncher
component "Node rendered-test wiring\ncanvas HTML and DOM output" as browserWiring
component "Rust xtask browser command\nbounded probe/render, stderr, child cleanup" as browserCommand
artifact "Selected Chromium executable\nlocked installation and version receipt" as browserExecutable
artifact "Owned capture session\nand code-server container" as captureProcesses
component "Modernization builder batch\nseparate from publication guard" as modernizationBatch
component "Rust xtask source identity\ntracked, new, deleted and instruction inputs\nbytes, file kind, link target, Unix executable bits" as sourceIdentity
artifact "External source-freeze manifest\ncreate once; outside the source checkout" as sourceManifest
component "Rust xtask database runner bridge\nsettings as data; replace inherited database settings" as databaseBridge
artifact "Disposable runner environment\ncredentials never printed" as databaseEnvironment
component "Existing real-database gate" as databaseGate
database "Local candidate state\nbranches and worktrees" as candidateState
component "Dependency exception check" as dependencyPolicy
component "VS Code npm audit" as npmAudit
artifact "Successful CI conformance artifact" as conformanceInput
component "Conformance status generator" as conformanceGenerator
component "Release provenance generator" as provenanceGenerator
component "Release claim contract" as claimContract
artifact "Release assets\nprovenance.json\nconformance.json/.md\nSHA256SUMS" as assets
database "Verification metadata\nspecs, gaps, invariants, proof" as verification

author --> productionDiff
author --> specificationDiff
author --> nativeTestDiff
author --> modernizationBatch : complete implementation and review
modernizationBatch --> sourceIdentity : freeze then verify source stability
sourceIdentity --> sourceManifest : create external snapshot
sourceManifest --> sourceIdentity : check frozen source
modernizationBatch --> databaseBridge : qualify affected driver graph
release --> databaseBridge : required real-product qualification
databaseEnvironment --> databaseBridge : decode and reject invalid entries
databaseBridge --> databaseGate : existing pinned products and CA
productionDiff --> prVerification
specificationDiff --> prVerification
nativeTestDiff --> prVerification
prVerification --> directChangeContract : enforce direct companions
directChangeContract --> release : candidate eligibility only after pass
runtimeCommsGate --> mosquitto : traffic-light symbolic mappings
mosquitto --> runtimeCommsGate : three topics change true and false\nno trust/io/in subscription
runtimeCommsGate --> conformanceInput : executable broker evidence
maintainer --> release : annotated tag
maintainer --> releaseGuard : verify release, then audit exact candidate
releaseGuard --> unsafeGate : require exact-source architecture evidence
unsafeGate --> unsafeFacts : external facts; Rust admission decision
releaseGuard --> captureLauncher : require exact-SHA capture result
releaseGuard --> browserWiring : unchanged rendered assertions
browserWiring --> browserCommand : executable and browser arguments
browserExecutable --> browserCommand : selected composition
browserCommand --> browserWiring : DOM output or explicit launch failure
captureLauncher --> captureProcesses : start and own
captureProcesses --> captureLauncher : reap on success, failure, or signal
releaseGuard --> release : query workflow, release, assets
releaseGuard --> candidateState : inspect ancestry, refs, dirtiness, and prunable registrations
candidateState --> releaseGuard : blockers or explicit cleanup targets
releaseGuard --> maintainer : blocked / cleanup required / clean
release --> dependencyPolicy : validate reviewed exceptions
release --> npmAudit : require zero lockfile advisories
release --> conformanceInput : download successful CI evidence
conformanceInput --> conformanceGenerator : suite result + commit
verification --> conformanceGenerator : known gaps and contract
release --> provenanceGenerator : tag, commit, workflow, artifacts
verification --> provenanceGenerator : platform and identity contract
conformanceGenerator --> claimContract : result-derived status
provenanceGenerator --> claimContract : artifact identity
claimContract --> assets : validate and checksum
release --> assets : publish only after all checks pass

note bottom of verification
  Targeted G1 proof supports implementation claims.
  Native, published, and device evidence remains required
  before public release claims close.
end note

note bottom of candidateState
  The audit never deletes automatically.
  Release handoff closes only after a clean rerun.
end note

note bottom of captureProcesses
  Reused external servers are not owned or terminated.
  Owned sessions and containers cannot survive the launcher.
end note

note bottom of directChangeContract
  Companion presence is necessary, not semantic proof.
  Executable workflows, crates, VS Code sources,
  scripts, xtask, and root build controls are covered.
  Owning specifications, native assertions, and reviewed
  behavior matrices remain the product authority.
end note

@enduml
